Kian OS is a Linux-based desktop operating system (Arch Linux base).

  * Real pacman:   pacman -Syu          (update)
                   pacman -S <pkg>      (install — needs internet)
  * Real Bash:     every GNU coreutils command works
  * Install:       sudo kianinstall     (Kian OS installer — our own fork of
                                        archinstall, works offline; set Disk first)
                   sudo kian-install    (same installer + auto Kian branding after)
  * Branding:      sudo kian-apply      (Kian files onto an installed Arch)
  * Sudo:          kian is in wheel; password is the user password
  * Login:         user `kian`, password `kian` (live session default)
  * Root login is disabled; privilege escalation is via sudo only.

Thanks for trying Kian OS — https://github.com/kiantaei/Kian-OS
